# `greatest` has an unboxed Body and an entry that visits the body itself. In that entry it ends in a direct tail call of `most`.
# `most` shares a call site with `least`, so it is boxed. It ends in a tail call of Math.max over an array, so no type is enforced on its result and that call has no entry check.
# Fault injection, testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Math.max/KindOfResult: the signature of Math.max declares null as its only result.
# The program used to print 0 instead of 0.5 and continue.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: 2
# CHECK-NEXT: 0.5
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: went on
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Math.max/KindOfResult
# LIE-NOT: went on
